<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13326" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē -saevĭo</span></b> ,
			ĭi (the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pluperfect subj.</i> contr. desaevisset,
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 29</span></i>), 4,
				v. n.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To rave furiously, to rage</i> (not anteAug., and
			very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">toto Aeneas desaevit in aequore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 569</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pelago hiems,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnes in artus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					6, 540</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 29</span></i>: tragica in arte,
			* <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 3, 14</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">belli Punici procella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					2, 6, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ira tua desaeviet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Num. 16, 22</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To cease raving</i> or <i>raging</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec dum desaeviat ira, Exspectat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					5, 304</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
